WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
00:00.360 --> 00:03.800
[This series contains scenes of violence, self-harm, and potential triggers.]

4
00:00.690 --> 00:01.800
Hey, hey, hey.

5
00:02.110 --> 00:04.860
Wake up. Stop playing dead.

6
00:03.800 --> 00:05.250
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

7
00:07.670 --> 00:09.340
Hey, is he really dead?

8
00:21.830 --> 00:23.390
Are you going to run away?

9
00:28.120 --> 00:30.080
119, what's your emergency?

10
00:30.330 --> 00:32.490
If you need help from 119...

11
00:32.810 --> 00:34.170
Are you running away?

12
00:34.560 --> 00:36.490
Are you planning to run away again?

13
00:38.860 --> 00:41.440
What do you want from me, you bastard?

14
00:43.680 --> 00:45.340
I told you I want you to sing.

15
00:45.670 --> 00:46.830
Join the audition.

16
00:47.990 --> 00:49.400
I'll help you get that song back.

17
00:49.400 --> 00:50.620
What right do you have to meddle?

18
00:50.620 --> 00:52.470
Shouldn't you be thrilled?

19
00:52.770 --> 00:54.890
I'm giving you another chance.

20
00:57.770 --> 00:59.450
If you run away again,

21
01:00.160 --> 01:01.700
it's really over.

22
01:02.190 --> 01:03.180
The end.

23
01:05.590 --> 01:06.980
You disgusting jerk.

24
01:10.840 --> 01:12.010
Forget it.

25
01:12.750 --> 01:16.210
Why should I waste my breath on a criminal who snoops on others?

26
01:20.140 --> 01:21.370
It's in three days.

27
01:23.200 --> 01:25.320
At the Midnight Art Hall.

28
01:40.060 --> 01:43.800
[Adapted from the webtoon "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

29
01:43.810 --> 01:46.600
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

30
01:46.610 --> 01:49.440
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

31
02:05.960 --> 02:07.450
[Yoo Dohyun]

32
02:07.460 --> 02:09.000
[Cho Chanhyeon]

33
02:09.050 --> 02:10.650
[Ko Gyeol]

34
02:12.650 --> 02:15.790
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

35
02:16.360 --> 02:17.890
If you run away again,

36
02:18.770 --> 02:19.980
it's really over.

37
02:20.620 --> 02:21.700
The end.

38
02:49.040 --> 02:49.980
Ah, ah, ah.

39
02:50.140 --> 02:51.940
Mic check, mic check.

40
02:52.000 --> 02:54.400
Lee Hanyul's vocal practice session for "Sound of Dawn"

41
02:54.400 --> 02:56.700
on July 26, 2026.

42
02:56.960 --> 02:58.890
Turn it off. Why are you recording?

43
02:59.070 --> 03:02.050
I'm going to sell it when you get famous.

44
03:02.280 --> 03:03.940
Yeah? Then pay me before you record.

45
03:03.940 --> 03:05.940
-No, I'm broke. -Then turn it off.

46
03:06.060 --> 03:07.000
No!

47
03:07.150 --> 03:08.610
-Turn it off! -Stay still.

48
03:08.810 --> 03:09.920
Just stay still.

49
03:09.920 --> 03:11.040
Ah, ah, ah.

50
03:11.350 --> 03:14.270
I'm Adolf, the one who wrote "Sound of Dawn."

51
03:14.600 --> 03:15.880
What are you doing?

52
03:16.280 --> 03:17.670
When this song becomes a hit,

53
03:17.670 --> 03:18.960
I'd become famous too.

54
03:19.090 --> 03:21.150
I'm just practicing for interviews.

55
03:21.150 --> 03:23.870
Oh my god. You really get ahead of yourself.

56
03:25.090 --> 03:27.090
By the way, is this thing recording?

57
03:27.210 --> 03:28.430
Ah, ah, ah.

58
03:29.380 --> 03:30.990
-Ah. -Lee Hanyul!

59
03:35.780 --> 03:38.720
Do you know why I wanted to be a songwriter?

60
03:39.860 --> 03:42.250
No surprise that you don't know.

61
03:42.530 --> 03:46.350
After my parents passed away, I kept having the same dream.

62
03:47.550 --> 03:52.210
In the dream, my parents would die over and over again.

63
03:53.540 --> 03:55.820
Do you remember how you'd sing to me

64
03:56.190 --> 03:58.790
every time I woke up from a nightmare

65
03:59.370 --> 04:01.710
and couldn't fall back asleep?

66
04:02.510 --> 04:04.150
Ever since then,

67
04:04.350 --> 04:06.360
every time I heard you sing,

68
04:06.580 --> 04:09.740
I felt like all my worries and sorrows vanished,

69
04:10.510 --> 04:13.170
and everything would be safe and sound forever.

70
04:14.030 --> 04:16.209
That's why I started writing songs.

71
04:16.680 --> 04:18.019
Because of you.

72
04:19.620 --> 04:24.070
I wanted everyone to hear your voice.

73
04:25.610 --> 04:27.170
You're a great singer.

74
04:28.780 --> 04:29.960
You got that?

75
04:30.270 --> 04:34.570
So promise me that no matter what happens, you'll keep singing.

76
04:35.300 --> 04:36.670
Pinky promise.

77
04:38.150 --> 04:39.680
Come on!

78
05:12.450 --> 05:16.350
[Song Choice: Sound of Dawn]

79
05:20.030 --> 05:21.360
You've got this, okay?

80
05:45.330 --> 05:46.510
Honey water.

81
05:52.590 --> 05:53.920
What are you doing?

82
05:53.920 --> 05:55.800
To speed up blood circulation.

83
05:55.810 --> 05:57.420
It calms your nerves.

84
06:01.260 --> 06:02.650
Why are you here?

85
06:03.460 --> 06:05.390
Look who's talking.

86
06:05.950 --> 06:07.560
I thought you wouldn't come.

87
06:07.830 --> 06:09.430
I didn't come for you.

88
06:10.630 --> 06:12.250
I came to get that song back.

89
06:12.400 --> 06:13.640
Whatever the reason.

90
06:14.440 --> 06:15.510
Good job.

91
06:15.790 --> 06:18.860
Contestants 90 to 100, please get ready.

92
06:44.560 --> 06:46.090
Can you make it?

93
06:48.750 --> 06:50.440
I'll do my part,

94
06:52.830 --> 06:55.110
so get ready to take that song back for me.

95
06:59.700 --> 07:01.010
Wait.

96
07:06.570 --> 07:07.740
What are you doing?

97
07:12.270 --> 07:13.360
Here.

98
07:15.230 --> 07:17.020
Call me if you advance.

99
07:17.370 --> 07:18.560
Good luck.

100
07:26.270 --> 07:29.090
Next is Contestant 99.

101
07:34.810 --> 07:36.580
What song have you prepared?

102
07:39.550 --> 07:40.950
Sound of Dawn.

103
07:41.140 --> 07:44.260
Oh. It's Herod's song.

104
07:44.970 --> 07:46.409
Adolf's song.

105
07:47.170 --> 07:48.080
Okay.

106
07:48.320 --> 07:49.530
You may begin.

107
07:52.180 --> 07:53.080
Okay.

108
07:53.790 --> 07:55.440
I'll help you get it back.

109
08:04.260 --> 08:08.580
Dawn always comes softly,

110
08:08.730 --> 08:12.620
leaving secret tears behind.

111
08:12.780 --> 08:14.680
The streets without you,

112
08:14.830 --> 08:16.660
the breeze without you—

113
08:16.800 --> 08:21.240
why does this night seem endless?

114
08:21.370 --> 08:24.850
Just once, just this once—

115
08:25.000 --> 08:31.690
if I could turn back time.

116
08:32.200 --> 08:34.679
The sound of dawn,

117
08:34.860 --> 08:38.659
my breath calling out to you.

118
08:39.669 --> 08:46.670
It may fade into the distance, yet it still reaches toward you.

119
08:48.380 --> 08:52.400
[Unspoken troubles? Nightscape is here to listen!]

120
08:52.410 --> 08:55.180
[Click for a Private Consultation]

121
08:58.930 --> 09:00.700
Herod, come check this out.

122
09:01.590 --> 09:03.870
I went to the Super Singer audition,

123
09:04.120 --> 09:07.180
and someone sang Sound of Dawn.

124
09:07.310 --> 09:09.000
His voice is crazy good.

125
09:09.300 --> 09:10.630
He totally killed it.

126
09:10.720 --> 09:12.050
Even better than yours.

127
09:12.170 --> 09:14.570
It's like the song was tailor-made for him.

128
09:15.040 --> 09:17.500
-Give it to me. -Dawn always comes softly...

129
09:17.800 --> 09:18.670
What do you think?

130
09:18.670 --> 09:19.700
He's insanely good, right?

131
09:19.700 --> 09:22.190
Leaving secret tears behind.

132
09:22.780 --> 09:25.240
Dawn always comes softly,

133
09:25.580 --> 09:29.600
leaving secret tears behind.

134
09:29.780 --> 09:31.540
The streets without you,

135
09:31.720 --> 09:33.660
the breeze without you—

136
09:33.810 --> 09:35.990
why does this night seem

137
09:35.990 --> 09:38.180
-endless? -Hello, Chairman.

138
09:38.400 --> 09:39.390
Just once...

139
09:41.460 --> 09:43.240
Oh, it's Mr. Lee.

140
09:43.600 --> 09:45.470
You're here, Boss.

141
09:46.740 --> 09:48.430
I'm not the boss, but the chairman.

142
09:48.430 --> 09:49.960
Call me Chairman, you brat.

143
09:50.350 --> 09:51.710
Yes, Chairman.

144
09:56.280 --> 09:58.080
Everything okay at the company?

145
09:58.290 --> 09:59.820
Are things going smoothly?

146
10:00.010 --> 10:01.480
Yes, they are.

147
10:03.300 --> 10:06.100
These are the newly signed collateral contracts.

148
10:06.980 --> 10:11.280
Goodness. If they were going to sell their kids for a few bucks,

149
10:11.290 --> 10:14.260
why did they go to all the trouble to conceive and raise them?

150
10:12.700 --> 10:15.030
[Collateral Contract Name: Kim Jaeseok]

151
10:15.320 --> 10:16.450
Don't you agree?

152
10:17.250 --> 10:18.510
Yes.

153
10:19.040 --> 10:20.510
Sift through them.

154
10:20.770 --> 10:23.000
Keep a few useful kids here,

155
10:23.040 --> 10:24.890
and transfer the rest to Mr. Han.

156
10:25.270 --> 10:26.870
Yes, noted.

157
10:28.180 --> 10:29.350
Right.

158
10:30.250 --> 10:33.810
What was the name of that kid who ran away?

159
10:34.680 --> 10:36.070
Han...

160
10:37.250 --> 10:38.530
It's Lee Hanyul.

161
10:38.850 --> 10:40.250
Right, him.

162
10:40.800 --> 10:42.660
Have we still not caught that kid?

163
10:43.960 --> 10:45.750
Yes, sorry.

164
10:46.310 --> 10:47.680
Oh, well.

165
10:48.760 --> 10:51.610
I wonder if that kid has any idea how much

166
10:51.750 --> 10:55.170
our dear Won has been suffering because of him.

167
10:59.130 --> 11:00.310
I'll leave you to it.

168
11:02.840 --> 11:04.030
Goodbye.

169
11:11.790 --> 11:16.150
[Safety Alert (Gangnam District Office) Roads may be icy tonight. Drive slowly.]

170
11:16.380 --> 11:18.810
[Delivery King: 5,000-won coupons for regulars. Check it out now!]

171
11:21.860 --> 11:23.720
[Delivery King: A deal you can't miss! Order now for free delivery!]

172
11:28.150 --> 11:31.100
[(Web Message) Exclusive benefits just for you! Click the link to find out.]

173
11:39.960 --> 11:41.280
Whatever.

174
11:45.460 --> 11:47.490
Your singing still sucks.

175
11:47.670 --> 11:49.320
Don't tell me you want to be a singer.

176
11:49.320 --> 11:50.590
Can you make it?

177
11:53.390 --> 11:55.430
What an annoying prick.

178
12:01.000 --> 12:04.110
[Super Singer Audition Team: You have passed the first round of auditions.]

179
12:04.120 --> 12:06.000
[2026 Super Singer: First-round audition qualifiers]

180
12:06.020 --> 12:07.430
[Lee Hanyul]

181
12:07.430 --> 12:09.900
[CEO: Lee Won]

182
12:19.380 --> 12:20.520
Come in!

183
12:25.190 --> 12:26.860
Why are you so disappointed?

184
12:27.040 --> 12:28.780
Are you waiting for someone?

185
12:30.920 --> 12:32.070
No.

186
12:32.350 --> 12:34.540
There's no way he'd come here anyway.

187
12:37.590 --> 12:39.480
[Hanyul: Are you free to meet?]

188
12:45.100 --> 12:46.720
You're still here?

189
12:47.170 --> 12:48.520
Leave if you're done.

190
12:49.010 --> 12:52.110
I haven't even started yet.

191
12:52.290 --> 12:53.620
Right, exactly! You...

192
12:53.780 --> 12:55.440
Why haven't you even started?

193
12:55.690 --> 12:58.530
Wait here. I have something urgent to deal with.

194
13:08.650 --> 13:09.940
I'm busy. What is it?

195
13:10.200 --> 13:11.600
Why did you want to see me?

196
13:11.750 --> 13:13.390
I passed the first round!

197
13:13.870 --> 13:14.920
So?

198
13:15.350 --> 13:16.380
Huh?

199
13:19.380 --> 13:22.140
Well, I just came to tell you this.

200
13:22.150 --> 13:24.040
Then you should prepare for the second round.

201
13:24.040 --> 13:25.190
Have you decided

202
13:25.520 --> 13:26.680
on a song?

203
13:27.060 --> 13:28.990
No, not yet.

204
13:29.900 --> 13:32.600
Remember the song you sang when you delivered food to me?

205
13:32.600 --> 13:34.530
The one you were humming casually.

206
13:35.610 --> 13:36.670
Sing that one.

207
13:37.230 --> 13:38.760
I'll take care of it myself.

208
13:38.870 --> 13:42.260
Sing that one. It suits your voice.

209
13:43.610 --> 13:46.800
Why are you helping me?

210
13:48.500 --> 13:50.360
Are you just getting curious now?

211
13:51.280 --> 13:55.080
Well... I'll tell you if you pass the second round.

212
13:55.550 --> 13:56.490
What?

213
13:56.720 --> 13:57.610
Why?

214
13:57.930 --> 13:59.310
Doubting yourself?

215
14:00.280 --> 14:03.470
Well, your reason for helping me doesn't matter anyway.

216
14:03.650 --> 14:06.180
Just be prepared to help me get that song back.

217
14:23.020 --> 14:24.220
Don't move.

218
14:26.770 --> 14:28.070
What are you doing?

219
14:31.780 --> 14:33.440
This is the practice room key.

220
14:33.460 --> 14:34.650
Go now.

221
14:35.060 --> 14:36.310
Focus on practicing.

222
15:37.320 --> 15:40.300
Your voice comes from here.

223
16:17.450 --> 16:18.520
Hey.

224
16:19.390 --> 16:20.690
What were you doing?

225
16:23.350 --> 16:25.420
Who told you to sleep with your mouth open?

226
16:25.420 --> 16:26.820
It's bad for your throat.

227
16:28.930 --> 16:30.220
Hurry up and get ready.

228
16:30.520 --> 16:31.850
You have your audition.

229
16:32.710 --> 16:33.800
Oh, right.

230
16:33.950 --> 16:35.030
What time is it?

231
16:36.260 --> 16:37.550
I'll take you.

232
16:38.380 --> 16:42.380
I'll speed up your blood circulation for you on the way to help you relax.

233
16:42.930 --> 16:44.580
I'll take care of it myself.

234
16:45.370 --> 16:46.650
Alright then.

235
16:49.450 --> 16:51.520
Oh, Lee Hanyul.

236
16:52.850 --> 16:55.560
Try to nail it this time too.

237
16:56.660 --> 16:58.620
For this second preliminary round,

238
16:58.620 --> 17:02.980
contestants must secure their secret judge's approval

239
17:03.130 --> 17:05.410
to clinch a spot in the finals.

240
17:34.140 --> 17:36.080
You're singing a song

241
17:36.230 --> 17:38.120
that I composed.

242
17:39.430 --> 17:41.230
You must be a fan of my songs.

243
17:42.590 --> 17:44.900
It's not me but my friend who likes them.

244
17:45.100 --> 17:47.160
[Song Choice: "Summer" by Lee Won] [Reason: It's my friend's favorite.]

245
17:48.040 --> 17:49.190
Alright.

246
17:49.360 --> 17:50.600
Let's hear it then.

247
18:01.620 --> 18:08.520
After the rain, the scent of the schoolyard slips through the window crack.

248
18:08.680 --> 18:12.320
We pass through the damp corridor,

249
18:12.500 --> 18:15.810
just walking silently all the way.

250
18:22.530 --> 18:24.570
You have a really nice voice.

251
18:31.290 --> 18:32.640
It's a no from me.

252
18:34.310 --> 18:36.440
You have a great voice.

253
18:36.580 --> 18:40.080
No, it's just your voice that is good,

254
18:40.450 --> 18:42.110
nothing more.

255
18:43.280 --> 18:45.730
You have zero understanding of the song.

256
18:47.340 --> 18:50.750
You've overestimated how good your voice actually is.

257
18:57.090 --> 18:58.530
You may leave.

258
19:15.810 --> 19:17.960
Try to nail it this time too.

259
19:19.510 --> 19:21.370
That jerk is unbelievable.

260
19:23.190 --> 19:24.870
Was this whole thing just to

261
19:25.040 --> 19:26.700
make a fool of me?

262
19:31.450 --> 19:34.110
You're not going to break it with your strength.

263
19:36.910 --> 19:38.130
You

264
19:38.700 --> 19:42.100
never actually planned to help me get that song back, did you?

265
19:42.230 --> 19:44.940
You'd made up your mind to eliminate me.

266
19:46.890 --> 19:49.860
I absolutely love your voice,

267
19:50.350 --> 19:52.890
so I'm thinking of training you properly.

268
19:53.230 --> 19:55.410
I despise half-hearted people.

269
19:55.860 --> 19:57.300
Enough with your crap.

270
19:59.010 --> 20:01.050
Do you find your elimination unfair,

271
20:01.050 --> 20:02.230
or did you

272
20:02.610 --> 20:05.810
really think you could make it to the finals at your level?

273
20:10.610 --> 20:11.720
This bodes well.

274
20:12.840 --> 20:15.120
This is what the audition was for.

275
20:15.820 --> 20:18.350
You had to see how much you were falling short.

276
20:18.700 --> 20:21.670
You must be thrilled that everything is going your way, huh?

277
20:21.670 --> 20:23.500
You really are a sickening bastard.

278
20:23.500 --> 20:24.830
Nothing has changed.

279
20:25.540 --> 20:28.570
I'll help you get that song back.

280
20:29.280 --> 20:31.590
You just need to keep singing.

281
20:36.960 --> 20:39.820
Wait, are you sick?

282
20:41.030 --> 20:42.330
None of your business.

283
20:49.320 --> 20:50.930
I'm not available now.

284
20:51.640 --> 20:53.500
Let's reschedule.

285
20:56.060 --> 20:57.410
I have nothing to say to you.

286
20:57.410 --> 20:58.520
I do.

287
20:58.600 --> 21:00.400
Just shut up and come with me.

288
21:07.400 --> 21:09.500
Don't you want to get that song back?

289
21:32.150 --> 21:35.010
It looks like he put a lot of work into this audition.

290
21:36.810 --> 21:37.670
Lee Hanyul.

291
21:37.860 --> 21:39.000
Get up.

292
21:39.030 --> 21:40.230
Eat something.

293
22:06.510 --> 22:08.440
Take medicine if you're sick.

294
22:08.610 --> 22:09.770
Are you stupid?

295
22:09.980 --> 22:11.550
It'll make me drowsy.

296
22:12.100 --> 22:13.240
Open your mouth.

297
22:13.680 --> 22:15.410
Stop it. I'm not a child.

298
22:15.850 --> 22:18.070
If you damage your voice, you won't hear the end of me.

299
22:18.070 --> 22:19.280
Open your mouth.

300
22:28.120 --> 22:29.090
Ah!

301
22:30.000 --> 22:31.180
It's so bitter.

302
22:32.250 --> 22:33.370
Are you a baby?

303
22:38.640 --> 22:40.700
Oh, please. Don't treat me like a kid.

304
22:44.480 --> 22:45.930
You're missing out.

305
23:16.260 --> 23:17.730
What are you doing?

306
23:58.730 --> 23:59.960
You

307
24:00.620 --> 24:02.020
were different from me.

308
24:01.950 --> 24:05.430
[Seven years ago]

309
24:08.090 --> 24:11.000
Unlike me, who was sold for a few bucks,

310
24:11.340 --> 24:13.530
you lived an ordinary life.

311
24:18.590 --> 24:21.450
So I thought it was a blessing.

312
24:31.110 --> 24:32.780
After all, your voice is

313
24:33.270 --> 24:35.870
more suited to an ordinary life.

314
24:41.860 --> 24:43.630
Somewhere along the way,

315
24:43.810 --> 24:45.930
music became your dream

316
24:46.090 --> 24:48.700
and became my whole universe.

317
25:11.590 --> 25:14.420
["Sound of Dawn" by Adolf]

318
25:26.970 --> 25:28.710
[All recordings: Hanyul's Song 32, Hanyul's Song 8]

319
25:41.820 --> 25:44.820
Somewhere along the way, your singing

320
25:45.480 --> 25:47.990
became my whole universe.

321
25:56.030 --> 25:59.510
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

322
25:59.520 --> 26:00.600
Your house's been put up for rent.

323
26:00.600 --> 26:01.610
What?

324
26:01.950 --> 26:03.360
It's all or nothing.

325
26:03.630 --> 26:04.580
Where are we?

326
26:04.750 --> 26:06.080
We have someone to meet.

327
26:06.100 --> 26:06.970
Who?

328
26:07.090 --> 26:08.050
Your vocal coach.

329
26:08.050 --> 26:09.050
Oh, Lee Won!

330
26:09.190 --> 26:10.680
Who's that cutie next to you?

331
26:10.680 --> 26:11.610
Your boyfriend?

332
26:11.640 --> 26:12.390
Huh?

333
26:12.410 --> 26:14.080
No! What are you talking about?

334
26:14.080 --> 26:15.330
Just trust me.

335
26:15.490 --> 26:18.040
Next, we're going to play hide-and-seek.

336
26:18.280 --> 26:20.220
Eh? Hide-and-seek?

337
26:20.350 --> 26:23.050
Fight against the wind.

338
26:23.190 --> 26:24.250
Next, stage three.

339
26:24.440 --> 26:25.860
Pour your feelings into the jajangmyeon.

340
26:25.860 --> 26:26.900
What?

341
26:26.950 --> 26:29.280
You've fallen for someone before, right?

342
26:30.770 --> 26:33.590
Where is he? Where is Lee Hanyul?

343
26:33.880 --> 26:35.320
You know, don't you!

344
26:35.320 --> 26:36.320
MkvDrama.net
